---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import StatusPill from '../components/StatusPill.astro';
import SovereigntyDiagram from '../components/SovereigntyDiagram.astro';
---
<Site
  title="Shamwari AI — an African AI companion that cites its sources"
  description="Shamwari is an AI companion built in Zimbabwe. It answers in Shona, Ndebele and English, cites the actual statute instead of guessing, and is built so your personal data can never reach a cloud model."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Community pillar of the Bundu Ecosystem</p>
    <h1>A friend that serves; a friend that does not control.</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Shamwari — Shona for <em>friend</em> — is an AI companion built in
      Zimbabwe. It answers in Shona, Ndebele and English, cites the actual
      provision of the actual statute instead of guessing, and is built so
      that anything it knows about <em>you</em> specifically can never leave
      your own device.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="https://docs.shamwari.ai">See how it's built</a>
      <a class="button" href="#contact">Get in touch</a>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-status"><StatusPill state="building" /> Pre-launch. We're building this in the open — see <a href="#status">where things actually stand</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wedge">
    <blockquote>Shamwari cites the Statutory Instrument. ChatGPT guesses.</blockquote>
    <p>
      Zimbabwean law, tax thresholds and monetary policy change most months.
      A model with that baked into its weights is stale the day it ships —
      and it will answer confidently anyway, because it has no way to know
      what it doesn't know. Shamwari retrieves the current text before it
      answers and shows you where the answer came from. The citation isn't a
      footnote. It's the product.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="what-it-is" class="band">
    <p class="eyebrow">What it is</p>
    <h2>One companion, three places it can run</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Shamwari isn't one model behind an API. It's three, and which one
      answers a question depends on whose question it is — not on which
      plan you're paying for.
    </p>

    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Cloud</h3>
        <p>Runs on routed third-party models. Fast, general knowledge, no
        persistent memory of you. Handles anything that isn't about your own
        life.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Ground</h3>
        <p>The Zimbabwean corpus — law, tax, regulation — kept fresh and
        cited by section. What makes an answer <em>correct</em> instead of
        just fluent.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Mind</h3>
        <p>A small, open-weight model that runs on your own device. The only
        thing that ever sees your personal data, because it never has to
        leave.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <SovereigntyDiagram>
      A question about your own life is answered on your device by Shamwari
      Mind. It is checked twice — once at the edge, once in the service that
      owns the data — because a leak here isn't an outage, it's a broken
      promise.
    </SovereigntyDiagram>

    <div class="rule">
      <p class="rule-title"><span class="rule-n">1</span> Your personal data never reaches a third-party model</p>
      <p>Not the cloud providers we route to, not anyone. If a question is
      about your own life and the only available answer would mean sending
      it to an outside model, Shamwari says so and stops — it does not
      quietly answer with a shrug instead. An honest "I can't help with that
      here" beats a confident answer that leaves something out.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rule">
      <p class="rule-title"><span class="rule-n">2</span> Only open-weight output trains Shamwari Mind</p>
      <p>The model we train and give away is never built from output whose
      licence forbids that. Every exchange is labelled the moment it's
      generated, and the training pipeline physically cannot ingest anything
      labelled otherwise.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="more-link"><a href="https://docs.shamwari.ai/rules/">Read the full detail, including how each rule is enforced in code →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="band alt">
    <p class="eyebrow">Ground — the moat</p>
    <h2>Freshness beats volume</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      A grounded small model beats an ungrounded large one on "what is the
      current PAYE threshold" — because the large one is guessing from
      memory and the small one is reading. We're building Ground as a living
      corpus with an effective date on every document, not a one-time
      scrape: when a Statutory Instrument supersedes an older one, retrieval
      stops citing the repealed version.
    </p>
    <p class="lede">
      What people actually ask becomes the roadmap for what we ingest next,
      starting with law, then tax and monetary policy, then agriculture and
      health once the sourcing is right.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="ecosystem" class="band">
    <p class="eyebrow">Ecosystem</p>
    <h2>Where Shamwari sits in the Bundu Ecosystem</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Bundu Foundation is a Zimbabwe-registered non-profit that holds the
      Shamwari IP and governs the wider ecosystem. Shamwari is sold
      commercially under Nyuchi Africa; the code itself stays Apache-2.0.
    </p>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card outline">
        <h3>Bundu Labs</h3>
        <p>Research.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card outline">
        <h3>Mukoko</h3>
        <p>The consumer super-app — several sub-apps currently running in
        beta across Africa.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card outline">
        <h3>Nyuchi Africa</h3>
        <p>The commercial pillar. Shamwari's paid tiers, and the wider
        Nyuchi product and services business, run here.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card outline highlight">
        <h3>Shamwari AI</h3>
        <p>The community pillar — this site. Free and open-weight at its
        core, because that's the version of the promise worth making.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band alt">
    <p class="eyebrow">Who it's for</p>
    <h2>Four ways to use it</h2>
    <div class="tiers">
      <div class="tier">
        <h3>Community</h3>
        <p class="tier-entity">Bundu Foundation</p>
        <p>Shamwari Mind, downloadable, open weights, forever free. This is
        the community pillar — not a trial of something else.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier">
        <h3>Developer</h3>
        <p class="tier-entity">Nyuchi Africa</p>
        <p>Pay-as-you-go API access to Shamwari Cloud, routed to the models
        that fit each request.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier">
        <h3>Business</h3>
        <p class="tier-entity">Nyuchi Africa</p>
        <p>Committed monthly volume, an SLA, and usage dashboards for teams
        building on top of Shamwari.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier">
        <h3>Sovereign</h3>
        <p class="tier-entity">Nyuchi Africa</p>
        <p>Mind and Ground deployed on your own infrastructure. No data
        leaves it, ever — for a ministry, a bank, or anyone else who needs
        that in writing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="lede small">
      We're inviting early customers in by hand rather than opening self-serve
      billing yet — see <a href="#contact">get in touch</a> below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="status" class="band">
    <p class="eyebrow">Where we are</p>
    <h2>Built in the open, honestly labelled</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      We'd rather this page be a little less impressive and stay true than
      round anything up. Here's what's actually running today versus what's
      still ahead.
    </p>
    <ul class="status-list">
      <li><StatusPill state="live" /> <strong>The architecture, in writing.</strong> <a href="https://docs.shamwari.ai">docs.shamwari.ai</a> documents exactly how routing, sovereignty and citation work, and it's checked against the real code.</li>
      <li><StatusPill state="live" /> <strong>Data sovereignty enforcement.</strong> The two rules above are live in code, enforced at more than one layer, and covered by tests — not policy on a page.</li>
      <li><StatusPill state="live" /> <strong>Ground's storage and search.</strong> The database and search indexes behind retrieval are running and ready.</li>
      <li><StatusPill state="building" /> <strong>The Zimbabwean legal and tax corpus.</strong> Sources are being reviewed and approved one at a time — we ingest what we have the rights to, nothing scraped first and asked about later. The Constitution of Zimbabwe is first in.</li>
      <li><StatusPill state="building" /> <strong>Shamwari Cloud.</strong> The gateway and API are written and tested, and not yet serving production traffic.</li>
      <li><StatusPill state="planned" /> <strong>Shamwari Mind.</strong> The on-device, open-weight model — the part that makes the sovereignty promise real for everyday use, not just for the API.</li>
      <li><StatusPill state="planned" /> <strong>Voice and image.</strong> Including Shona and Ndebele speech, once a provider actually supports them well.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="band alt contact">
    <p class="eyebrow">Get in touch</p>
    <h2>Talk to us before you talk to a consultant</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      We're bringing on the first customers by hand — mostly around
      Zimbabwean tax and regulatory compliance, where being wrong costs real
      money and the answer changes monthly. If that's you, if you want early
      access to Ground once it opens up, or if you're a Zimbabwean legal or
      language source who wants to talk about a licence, say hello.
    </p>
    <a class="button primary large" href="mailto:hello@shamwari.ai">hello@shamwari.ai</a>
  </section>
</Site>

<style>
  section { max-width: 72rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sodalite);
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.4vw, 2rem); line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 1rem; text-wrap: balance;
  }
  h3 {
    font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.02rem;
    color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .lede { max-width: var(--measure); color: var(--text); margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
  .lede.small { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--granite); }

  .hero { padding: 4rem 1.5rem 3rem; }
  .hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 3.4rem); line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--ink); margin: 0.3rem 0 1.1rem;
    max-width: 20ch; text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .standfirst { max-width: var(--measure); font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--granite); margin: 0 0 1.75rem; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .hero-status { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--granite); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  .button {
    display: inline-block; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem;
    padding: 0.7em 1.3em; border-radius: 3px; border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    color: var(--ink); background: var(--surface);
  }
  .button:hover { border-color: var(--sodalite); color: var(--sodalite); }
  .button.primary { background: var(--sodalite); border-color: var(--sodalite); color: var(--surface); }
  .button.primary:hover { background: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--surface); }
  .button.large { font-size: 1.05rem; padding: 0.85em 1.6em; }

  .wedge { padding: 1rem 1.5rem 3.5rem; }
  .wedge blockquote {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem; padding-left: 1.1rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--sodalite);
    font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--sodalite); max-width: 34ch;
  }
  .wedge p { max-width: var(--measure); color: var(--text); margin: 0; }

  .band { padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem; }
  .band.alt { background: var(--surface); max-width: 100%; }
  .band.alt > * { max-width: 72rem; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }

  .grid-3 { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; margin-bottom: 2.25rem; }
  .grid-2 { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 42rem) {
    .grid-3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
    .grid-2 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  .card { padding: 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 4px; background: var(--surface); }
  .card p { margin: 0; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .card.outline { background: transparent; }
  .card.outline.highlight { border-color: var(--sodalite); background: var(--sodalite-q); }

  .rule { max-width: var(--measure); margin: 0 0 1.25rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem; border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-left: 3px solid var(--sodalite); border-radius: 2px; }
  .rule-title { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .rule-n {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    width: 1.4em; height: 1.4em; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--sodalite); color: var(--surface);
    font-size: 0.8rem; flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .rule p:last-child { margin: 0; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .more-link { font-size: 0.92rem; }

  .tiers { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  @media (min-width: 50rem) { .tiers { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); } }
  .tier { padding: 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 4px; background: var(--paper); }
  .tier-entity { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--granite); }
  .tier p:last-child { margin: 0; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text); }

  .status-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.9rem; max-width: var(--measure); }
  .status-list li { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.7rem; flex-wrap: wrap; color: var(--text); }
  .status-list strong { color: var(--ink); }

  .contact { text-align: left; }
</style>
